FIXED: shared/system.css, shared/kinetic.js
  — Respect system preferences (reduced motion) and the site's own Effects switch
  — The name's colour drift and pencil wobble now stop when Effects is switched off or reduced motion is chosen mid-visit (they used to keep going until the page was reloaded)
FIXED: index-src.html (seek bars of the mini and full-screen players)
  — Screen reader announcements: a control must state its current value
  — The seek slider no longer reads "Nothing playing" during a song; it now reports "1:00 of 2:57" on load, play, pause, jump and every 15 s (not while focused, to avoid talking over the music)
FIXED: index-src.html (player cover images)
  — Meaningful contextual text: alt text must describe the image; decorative images get alt=""
  — The full-screen player's cover is now described as "Album cover: <album name>" instead of the placeholder "Now playing"; the mini player's cover (inside an already-named button) is marked decorative
FIXED: shared/system.css (touch targets)
  — Keyboard and pointer operability: controls must be large enough to press (the site's own rule: 44px on touch)
  — On touch screens the streaming, YouTube and email buttons, the full-screen player's controls, the per-track lyrics buttons, the lyric lines and the skip link grow from 40px to 44px; mouse screens are unchanged
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (settings switches in the menu)
  — Screen reader semantics + pattern documentation: a control's name and its description are separate things
  — Each switch is now announced as "Effects, switch, on" with its explanation as the description, instead of one run-together name ("Single-key shortcutsG then a letter…"); the switch and fold patterns are documented in the component's comments
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (menu dialog, initial focus)
  — Keyboard operability: focus order must be safe and predictable; pattern documented in the component
  — Opening the menu by keyboard now puts focus on the first section button (or first setting on wide screens) instead of the "Listen on Apple Music" link, where a second press of Enter would have left the site
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (setting descriptions)
  — Accessible content: instructions in plain, complete sentences
  — "G then a letter to jump to a section, / to search" is now "Press G, then the first letter of a section, to jump to it. Press / to search."; "Xylophone notes when you press" is now "Plays a short note when you press a button"
